clinic with a complaint of headaches 3 to 5
days before her period. The headache often
Starts from the back of her head (occipital
area) and radiates to her left temple. It is
aggravated by walking or other types of
physical activity. She denies visual, auditory,
or taste disturbances but mentions that she
cannot tolerate noisy or crowded places
during attacks. According to her, every
headache episode lasts from two to several
hours. Physical examination, including a
complete neurological exam, is inconclusive.
Which one of the following could be the most
likely diagnosis?',NULL,'B',NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-24035941e106","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"9cd229628d4f6a09095a","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","source_page":136,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"9cd229628d4f6a09095a","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":136,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Neurology","stem":"A 30-year-old woman presents to your GP\nclinic with a complaint of headaches 3 to 5\ndays before her period. The headache often\nStarts from the back of her head (occipital\narea) and radiates to her left temple. It is\naggravated by walking or other types of\nphysical activity. She denies visual, auditory,\nor taste disturbances but mentions that she\ncannot tolerate noisy or crowded places\nduring attacks. According to her, every\nheadache episode lasts from two to several\nhours. Physical examination, including a\ncomplete neurological exam, is inconclusive.\nWhich one of the following could be the most\nlikely diagnosis?","options":{},"source_answer":"B","source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"source_revealed","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"low","currentness_keywords":[],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"medium","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-0