leg. His past medical history is significant for
coronary angioplasty 5 years ago for which he
is currently on daily low-dose aspirin. A non-
contrast brain CT scan excludes cerebral
hemorrhage. Doppler ultrasonography shows
bilateral carotid artery stenosis of 50%. Which
one of the following would be the most
