complaint of recurrent episodes of vertigo. She
describes that she has had these episode every
month for the past five years. The vertigo is
followed by imbalance and sometimes nausea
and vomiting. She denies any hearing
impairment or ringing in the ear, or ear fullness
during the attacks. She is otherwise healthy and
does not drink alcohol or smoke. Physical
examination is unremarkable. Which one of the
following would be the most appropriate
management for her?','{"A":"Refer her to ENT specialist.","B":"_Reassure her that this is a\nbenign condition.","C":"Tempanostomy.","D":"Prescribe decongestants.","E":"MRI of the posterior fossa."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-b8235b8cd5f3","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"43545a378326f31f1b5f","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","source_page":155,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"7fac7190e7b76f8718c2","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","source_page":154,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"9b2dd027ceff8abe049d","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":788,"source_qid":"1379"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"43545a378326f31f1b5f","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":155,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Neurology","stem":"A 21-year-old woman is in your GP clinic with\ncomplaint of recurrent episodes of vertigo. She\ndescribes that she has had these episode every\nmonth for the past five years. The vertigo is\nfollowed by imbalance and sometimes nausea\nand vomiting. She denies any hearing\nimpairment or ringing in the ear, or ear fullness\nduring the attacks. She is otherwise healthy and\ndoes not drink alcohol or smoke. Physical\nexamination is unremarkable. Which one of the\nfollowing woul