Covid19 vaccine. Now, she has presented with
complaints of persistent headaches, anorexia,
and nausea. The headache has been resistant
to painkillers and progressive. He has no other
symptoms and has been otherwise in good
health. She only takes thyroxine for
hypothyroidism.
On examination, she is systemically well and
has a blood pressure (BP) of 130/75 mmHg
while lying down, a regular pulse rate of 78
beats per minute, a respiratory rate of 16
breaths per minute, and oxygen saturation of
98% on room air. The ear, nose, and throat
examinations are unremarkable, as is the
cardiovascular exam. A full neurological exam
was performed, and no findings were
concerning. She has a Glasgow coma scale
(GCS) of 15. Which one of the following is the
most important investigation to perform’?','{"A":"24-hour BP monitoring.","B":"CT scan of the head.","C":"D-Dimers, fibrinogen, and platelet levels.","D":"Urgent retinal scans.","E":"Radionucleotide imaging of the thyroid."}','C',NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","supporting_pages":[158],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-0d6598ed89a4","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"145bacab7ee7f3dcaa91","record_type":"visual_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","source_page":158,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.8.2-residual-resolver-page-checkpoint-local-render-2026-09-23","parser_mode":"v282_visual_page_asset","text_method":"source_page_image+best_available_text","visual_asset":"visual_assets/AMEDEX_2025_NEUROLOGY_2__d3816bb7b8b9/page_00158.jpg","asset_preview_url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_lceFWxZKxvFPeqfe_Ag1KDD3ZGvLp7Z/preview"}','visual_assets/AMEDEX_2025_NEUROLOGY_2__d3816bb7b8b9/page_00158.jpg','https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1_lceFWxZKxvFPeqfe_Ag1KDD3ZGvLp7Z&sz=w1600','source_page_image',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"145bacab7ee7f3dcaa91","record_type":"visual_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (2).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":158,"supporting_pages":[158],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Neurology","stem":"Ten days ago, Jenna, 65 years old, received\nCovid19 vaccine. Now, she has presented with\ncomplaints of persistent headaches, anorexia,\nand nausea. The headache has been resistant\nto painkillers and progressive. He has no other\nsymptoms and has been otherwise in good\nhealth. She only takes thyroxine for\nhypothyroidism.\nOn examination, she is systemically well and\nhas a blood pressure (BP) of 130/75 mmHg\nwhile lying down, a regular pulse rate of 78\nbeats per minute, a respiratory rat