recurrent visual problems. She describes that
she frequently experiences glimmering flashes
in her vision for about 10 to 15 minutes each
time, which are entirely resolved every time.
She also has experienced global headaches,
which worsen with exertion. Visual acuity, visual
fields, eye movements and pupillary reflexes
are normal on examination. The fundoscopic
examination is inconclusive. There are no focal
neurological deficits on central nervous system
examination either. Which one of the following
could be the most likely diagnosis?','{"A":"Focal epilepsy.","B":"Occipital lobe tumour.","C":"Optic neuritis.","D":"Migraine with aura.","E":"x — Carotid artery stenosis."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (3).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-3092da751b31","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"e2b8fb783cabe3951298","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (3).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (3).pdf","source_page":76,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"2c5569d76bc3b0c03dfe","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (3).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (3).pdf","source_page":75,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"e2b8fb783cabe3951298","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (3).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 NEUROLOGY (3).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":76,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Neurology","stem":"A 26-year-old woman presents with a history of\nrecurrent visual problems. She describes that\nshe frequently experiences glimmering flashes\nin her vision for about 10 to 15 minutes each\ntime, which are entirely resolved every time.\nShe also has experienced global headaches,\nwhich worsen with exertion. Visual acuity, visual\nfields, eye movements and pupillary reflexes\nare normal on examination. The fundoscopic\nexamination is inconclusive. There are no focal\nneurological deficits on central nervous system\nexamination either. Which one of the following\ncould be the most likely diagnosis?","options":{"A":"Focal epilepsy.","B":"Occipital lobe tumour.","C":"Optic neuritis.","D":"Migraine with aura.